  "author_association": "NONE",
  "body": "H and L will cooperate to try their best to make answers exactly the same as the labels in the dataset if the original loss function is kept. I tried this on wikitext-2-v1, using the same evaluation metrics. I found that after just a few epochs of training, the model can achieve an accuracy of over 50% on the test set.\n\nIf I'm understanding the model and metrics correctly, it seems that HRM can efficiently learn to answer purely textual questions exactly as they appear in the dataset. I'm curious if there's an upper limit to this performance. Will the model only eventually overfits on these purely text-based tasks? I think this is worth more investigating.\n",
